# Newline-separated regexes for file paths to exclude from secret scanning.
# Consulted by the secret-scan job (full history, all detectors, unverified
# included) to silence known false positives.

# Connection-string placeholder examples (Password=..., Password=<secret>) in a
# deleted enterprise infra doc. SQLServer detector flags these as unverified.
^docs/aws\.md$

# The SQLite-to-Postgres migration procedure documents the --target connection
# string and the DB_CONNECTION_STRING it maps to, so a Host=...;Password=... form
# is the thing being explained and cannot be paraphrased away. The SQLServer
# detector flags the placeholder as unverified, same shape as docs/aws.md.
^docs/sqlite-to-postgres-migration\.md$

# The secret-scan walks full history across all branches. Exclude this allowlist
# file from its own scan so placeholder examples in these comments are not
# re-flagged by the URI detector.
^\.trufflehog-exclude$

# apk Basic-auth doc-comment placeholder (URL userinfo form) is not a credential.
# It lives in apk ecosystem commit history, which the full-history scan walks.
^src/Dependably\.Core/Api/ApkController\.cs$
^tests/Dependably\.Tests/Integration/ApkControllerTests\.cs$

# Fixed URL-userinfo placeholders in the upstream-credential-stripping tests. The
# [InlineData] cases assert that a scheme://user:pass@host upstream has its
# credentials redacted, so the placeholder form is the fixture under test — not a
# real secret. Attribute arguments must be compile-time constants, so the literal
# cannot be broken up by interpolation the way the integration fixture does.
^tests/Dependably\.Tests/Unit/SecurityTests\.cs$
^tests/Dependably\.Tests/Unit/Api/UpstreamRegistryControllerAuthTests\.cs$
